# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and FILL IN: copying it blank is worse than not having it at all. Read by the Cloudflare Vite
# plugin / `wrangler dev`.
#
# An empty `KEY=` line is a DEFINED empty string, not an absent value, so it shadows whatever `shopify app dev` injects. That is why
# SHOPIFY_API_SECRET is not listed below: `npm run dev` injects it (with SHOPIFY_API_KEY, SCOPES and the tunnel URL).
#
# Secret NAMES are declared in wrangler.jsonc (`secrets.required`), so `wrangler types` does not need this file: a fresh clone compiles
# with no `.dev.vars` at all.

# Signs the links of support attachments. Any long random string locally.
ATTACHMENT_TOKEN_SECRET=dev-attachment-secret

# Keys the address hashes of the notify kernel and signs every unsubscribe link (at least 32 characters). REQUIRED: the preset refuses to build its services without it.
# Locally anything long enough; in production `wrangler secret put NOTIFY_SECRET --env production` (openssl rand -base64 32) and never change it afterwards
# (a new value makes every unsubscribe link already sent invalid and every stored address hash unmatched).
NOTIFY_SECRET=dev-notify-secret-of-at-least-thirty-two-characters

# Development only: limit EVERY mail the app sends to these addresses (or @domains), comma separated, so a test shop's real customers never receive one. Unset = no limit.
# NOTIFY_DEV_ALLOW=you@example.com,@yourcompany.com

# The HMAC key every app and the portal hash events with (at least 32 characters). Locally anything long enough; production uses the shared secret and EVENT_HASH_KEY_ID.
EVENT_HASH_SECRET=dev-event-hash-secret-of-at-least-thirty-two-characters

# Partner API token (reads this app's subscription). Empty = the subscription refresh reports `not_configured` and the shop stays on the
# free plan. Needs PARTNER_ORG_ID and PARTNER_APP_ID (vars in wrangler.jsonc; the Partner Dashboard URL and the app overview).
# PARTNER_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: Cloudflare Turnstile secret for the public support form (the site key is TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY in wrangler.jsonc). Empty = check off.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional: seals the `secret()` fields of `@firesio/app/settings` at rest (AES-256-GCM): base64 of 32 random bytes, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`.
# Only an app that declares `settings` has any use for it; empty = stored as plain text, and adding it later needs no migration (the next save
# seals the row). SETTINGS_SECRET_KEY_ID (default s1) names it; SETTINGS_SECRET_KEY_PREVIOUS and its _ID serve a rotation. In production:
# `wrangler secret put SETTINGS_SECRET_KEY --env production`.
# SETTINGS_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional: custom shop domains Shopify may authenticate (a comma list is not supported: one domain).
# SHOP_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=

# Transactional email (`app/notifications/streams.ts`): notification@ and support@ the app's domain, the host of SHOPIFY_APP_URL once deployed.
# Locally (a tunnel URL) set MAIL_DOMAIN in wrangler.jsonc vars to a domain onboarded to Email Sending; with no domain every mail is recorded
# as `skipped:no_sender`, never an error:
#   npx wrangler email sending enable yourdomain.com
# The binding is not `remote` in wrangler.jsonc, so a send during `npm run dev` (and in tests) is SIMULATED by Miniflare: nothing is delivered
# and no `wrangler login` is needed. Only a deployed Worker sends real mail.

# NOTE: never set SHOPIFY_APP_URL here: it would shadow the live tunnel URL that `shopify app dev` injects.

# The App Store listing handle (apps.shopify.com/<handle>). Leave it unset locally and before the app is listed: the landing page then
# shows the shop-domain install form. Setting it makes every Install button link to the listing and hides the form.
# SHOPIFY_APP_HANDLE=
